{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00793",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.28,
      "end_seconds": 9.39,
      "duration_seconds": 8.11,
      "text": "Hello. Er, it's my migraines. The preventers, the tablets, they don't seem to be doing much."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 11.95,
      "end_seconds": 16.25,
      "duration_seconds": 4.3,
      "text": "How often are you getting migraines now?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 18.64,
      "end_seconds": 27.31,
      "duration_seconds": 8.67,
      "text": "Maybe, ooh, six or seven a month? It was eight before, so not much of a change."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 29.65,
      "end_seconds": 35.92,
      "duration_seconds": 6.27,
      "text": "How long do they last, and what are they like?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 38.85,
      "end_seconds": 47.74,
      "duration_seconds": 8.89,
      "text": "One side, throbbing, with light bothering me, and I feel sick. Eight hours, sometimes a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 50.04,
      "end_seconds": 55.06,
      "duration_seconds": 5.02,
      "text": "When did they get worse, can you say?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 57.86,
      "end_seconds": 65.78,
      "duration_seconds": 7.92,
      "text": "Um. A year ago? Or since the new job? I really couldn't say when they changed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 67.25,
      "end_seconds": 73.23,
      "duration_seconds": 5.98,
      "text": "That's fine. Any aura, flashing lights, or zigzags, before them?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 75.4,
      "end_seconds": 77.99,
      "duration_seconds": 2.59,
      "text": "No. None of that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 80.28,
      "end_seconds": 84.17,
      "duration_seconds": 3.89,
      "text": "What are you taking to prevent them?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 86.36,
      "end_seconds": 102.75,
      "duration_seconds": 16.39,
      "text": "Propranolol, 80 mg twice a day. I think. And topiramate, 50 mg once a day, at night, but I forget it a lot. And sumatriptan, 50 mg, when I get one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 106.04,
      "end_seconds": 118.32,
      "duration_seconds": 12.28,
      "text": "So the topiramate is prescribed daily, but you often miss it. It's difficult to judge if it's working then. Any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 120.56,
      "end_seconds": 122.39,
      "duration_seconds": 1.83,
      "text": "No, none."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 125.56,
      "end_seconds": 128.52,
      "duration_seconds": 2.96,
      "text": "And your medical history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 129.92,
      "end_seconds": 136.6,
      "duration_seconds": 6.68,
      "text": "Migraines since I was a teenager, and I get anxious sometimes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 139.39,
      "end_seconds": 143.48,
      "duration_seconds": 4.09,
      "text": "Do you drink coffee, how's your sleep?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 145.26,
      "end_seconds": 151.47,
      "duration_seconds": 6.21,
      "text": "Four coffees a day. And I sleep terribly, five or six hours."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 153.28,
      "end_seconds": 158.86,
      "duration_seconds": 5.58,
      "text": "Let me check your pulse and blood pressure. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 162.1,
      "end_seconds": 163.79,
      "duration_seconds": 1.69,
      "text": "Okay. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 176.78,
      "end_seconds": 181.49,
      "duration_seconds": 4.71,
      "text": "Pulse 62, blood pressure 112 over 70, temperature 36.6."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 184.88,
      "end_seconds": 186.83,
      "duration_seconds": 1.95,
      "text": "All right? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 189.6,
      "end_seconds": 197.77,
      "duration_seconds": 8.17,
      "text": "All fine. The propranolol slows the pulse, as expected. Any breathlessness, wheeze, or cold hands?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 200.43,
      "end_seconds": 203.38,
      "duration_seconds": 2.95,
      "text": "No, nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 205.85,
      "end_seconds": 223.07,
      "duration_seconds": 17.22,
      "text": "So here's what I think. You've got migraines about six or seven a month, and you're missing the topiramate often, so I'd say these migraines are not well controlled, partly because the preventer isn't being taken regularly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 225.99,
      "end_seconds": 230.71,
      "duration_seconds": 4.72,
      "text": "I know. I'm rubbish at tablets. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 233.36,
      "end_seconds": 246.95,
      "duration_seconds": 13.59,
      "text": "A lot of people are. The best step is to make the routine easier, so take it in the evening, with your teeth-cleaning, and set a phone reminder."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 250.0,
      "end_seconds": 253.06,
      "duration_seconds": 3.06,
      "text": "That's a good idea. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 255.93,
      "end_seconds": 265.01,
      "duration_seconds": 9.08,
      "text": "Keep a migraine diary for a month, noting triggers, such as coffee, sleep and skipped meals."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 268.1,
      "end_seconds": 271.81,
      "duration_seconds": 3.71,
      "text": "I'll download an app. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 275.08,
      "end_seconds": 282.15,
      "duration_seconds": 7.07,
      "text": "And cut your coffee to two cups, and get regular sleep. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 284.59,
      "end_seconds": 286.64,
      "duration_seconds": 2.05,
      "text": "Right. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 288.16,
      "end_seconds": 300.11,
      "duration_seconds": 11.95,
      "text": "I'd like to see you in six weeks, to review the diary and decide whether to change the treatment."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 302.63,
      "end_seconds": 306.0,
      "duration_seconds": 3.37,
      "text": "Six weeks. Thank you. ~"
    }
  ]
}
